  {
    "description": "Notion | Create a file upload
Step 1 of attaching a file to Notion. Reserves an upload and returns an \`id\`. Then call \`API-send-a-file-upload\` with that id to transfer the bytes, and finally reference it from a block or property as \`{"type": "file_upload", "file_upload": {"id": "<id>"}}\`. Single-part uploads are limited to 20MB. An upload must be attached within one hour or it expires.",
    "httpMethod": "post",
    "name": "create-a-file-upload",
    "properties": [
      "content_type",
      "external_url",
      "filename",
      "mode",
    ],
    "required": [],
  },
  {
    "description": "Notion | Create a view
Create a view over a data source: a table, board, calendar, timeline, gallery, list, form, chart, map or dashboard, with its own filter, sorts and layout. Exactly one of \`database_id\`, \`view_id\` or \`create_database\` must be given — \`database_id\` adds a tab to an existing database, \`view_id\` adds a widget to an existing dashboard, and \`create_database\` puts a linked view of an existing data source on a page. Note that \`database_id\` and \`data_source_id\` are different IDs and both are needed: retrieve the database to find its \`data_sources\` array. \`configuration.type\` must equal the view's \`type\`, and a board view must carry a \`group_by\`.
Error Responses:
400: Bad request",
    "httpMethod": "post",
    "name": "create-a-view",
    "properties": [
      "configuration",
      "create_database",
      "data_source_id",
      "database_id",
      "filter",
      "name",
      "placement",
      "position",
      "quick_filters",
      "sorts",
      "type",
      "view_id",
    ],
    "required": [
      "data_source_id",
      "name",
      "type",
    ],
  },
  {
    "description": "Notion | Create a view query
Run a view's saved filter and sort and get the first page of matching pages back, so you see what a person looking at that view sees without rebuilding its filter logic yourself. The response carries the results plus a \`query_id\`, \`total_count\` and \`has_more\`; use Get view query results with that \`query_id\` to page through the rest. The cached result set expires on its own after about 15 minutes.
Error Responses:
400: Bad request",
    "httpMethod": "post",
    "name": "create-a-view-query",
    "properties": [
      "page_size",
      "view_id",
    ],
    "required": [
