  {
    "description": "Notion | Delete a comment permanently. This cannot be undone — a deleted comment is gone for good, with no trash to restore it from. Deletes exactly one comment, named by its id.
Error Responses:
400: Bad request
403: Forbidden — the integration lacks the insert-comment capability
404: Not found — no such comment, or it was created by someone else",
    "httpMethod": "delete",
    "name": "delete-a-comment",
    "properties": [
      "comment_id",
    ],
    "required": [
      "comment_id",
    ],
  },
  {
    "description": "Notion | Delete a view
Permanently remove a view from its database. This cannot be undone through the API. A database must keep at least one view, so deleting the last one fails with a validation error — to get rid of the database itself, set \`in_trash\` on the database instead. The response is a partial view object with only \`object\`, \`id\`, \`parent\` and \`type\`, since the view no longer exists to describe.
Error Responses:
400: Bad request",
    "httpMethod": "delete",
    "name": "delete-a-view",
    "properties": [
      "view_id",
    ],
    "required": [
      "view_id",
    ],
  },
  {
    "description": "Notion | Delete a view query
Release a cached view query once you have finished paging through it. Optional housekeeping — a query expires by itself after about 15 minutes — but worth doing when queries are run often. It deletes only the cached result set; the view and its pages are untouched.
Error Responses:
400: Bad request",
    "httpMethod": "delete",
